+# ISURIDE deployment
+
+- **s1:** nginx HTTPS and static files, HTTP/2, precompressed assets, large connection/file limits. Proxies APIs to s3:8080.
+- **s2:** main MySQL database: users, chairs, rides, status history, coupons and payment configuration.
+- **s3:** Go application plus separate local MySQL location store. `isuride-go.service` and MySQL start automatically.
+- The original external matching services are disabled. The application runs its matcher every 25 ms.
+
+The Go application maintains a read model populated from MySQL at startup and rebuilt during initialization. Successful mutations update the read model after database persistence. Coordinate updates and notification acknowledgments are batched; callers wait for their writes. Latest coordinates and exact accumulated distances are persisted in `chair_state`. Notification status histories and delivery flags remain durable in the main database. Payments use a per-ride idempotency key.
+
+Matching considers pickup travel time, trip distance, model speed and increasing wait priority. Assignments are persisted in batches. SSE delivers each queued status in order. Read APIs use the committed read model.
+
+Current source: `webapp/go/`. Initialization scripts: `webapp/sql/`. Deployed configuration snapshots and persistence checker: `config/`. Benchmark output: `results/run01.txt` through `results/run15.txt`.
+
+Build on s3:
+
+```sh
+cd /home/isucon/webapp/go
+/home/isucon/local/golang/bin/go build -o isuride.new .
+/home/isucon/local/golang/bin/go vet ./...
+sudo systemctl stop isuride-go
+mv isuride.new isuride
+sudo systemctl start isuride-go
+```
+
+Verification before final run:
+
+- All three servers rebooted; enabled services started and frontend/API responded.
+- 500 coordinate updates exercised durable location storage.
+- 40 sampled owner sales, chair details and user ride histories matched across restart after fixing timestamp precision.
+- Precompressed JavaScript decompresses to the original SHA-256 digest.
+- Go build, `go vet`, nginx configuration checks and `git diff --check` passed.
+- Best tuning result was run 13: PASS, 606,582. Run 14 passed at 568,777; the run-13 matching penalty was restored for the final run.
